CATEGORIES: Featuring,MAP,CBD
DTSTAMP:20260806T130504Z
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating National Handloom Day\, we have Vaishnavi Kambadur and Mamatha G P K introducing us to the history and mechanics of handlooms. \n\nThe session explores the cultural and social story of the cloth\, its smell (natural dyes like Kalamkari and indigo)\, motifs (Ikat\, Bandhani\, Ajrakh)\, historic revivals (Chintz\, Baluchari)\, the weaving communities and castes behind specific textiles (Banarasi\, Pochampally\, Jamdani)\, and regional origins (Patola\, Chanderi\, Kanjeevaram).\n\nFollowing this\, it covers the technical side\, its loom types (pit\, frame\, shuttle\, jacquard)\, fabric count (Muslin vs. khadi)\, and hand vs. power loom distinctions. Having covered the history\, the session dives into handlooms in contemporary culture\, their presence in film costuming and social media trends like converting sarees into western silhouettes. The programme concludes with interactive session identifying different textiles and swatches from the MAP collection.\n\n&nbsp\;
DTEND:20260807T130000Z
DTSTART:20260807T113000Z
SUMMARY:Between the Looms - The Hands that Time Unearthed
UID:1358@map-india.org
URL:https://map-india.org/map-events/between-the-looms/
END:VEVENT
