DESCRIPTION:                                                  Tvarita Arts Collective India \n\nJarasandha Vadhe is a well-known story from the Mahabharata. To help Yudhishthira perform the Rajasuya Yajna\, Lord Krishna\, along with Bhima and Arjuna\, visits the powerful King Jarasandha of Magadha. A fierce duel follows between Bhima and Jarasandha\, ending with the victory of good over evil through Krishna's guidance and Bhima's strength.\n\nThis Yakshagana performance features four iconic characters - Krishna\, Jarasandha\, Bhima\, and Arjuna and brings the story to life through expressive acting\, traditional music\, vibrant costumes\, and energetic dance. Presented by Team Yakshadegula\, the performance is uniquely brought to life by an ensemble of women Yakshagana artists\, celebrating both the richness of this classical storytelling tradition and the growing presence of women in the art form. \n\nThe performance is curated by Tvarita Arts Collective India. \n\nThis event is in conjunction with programming for Grip\, Hold\, Pin. 
DTEND:20260816T140000Z
DTSTART:20260816T130000Z
SUMMARY:Jarasandha Vadhe - Yakshagana Performance
UID:1371@map-india.org
URL:https://map-india.org/map-events/jarasandha-vadhe-yakshagana-performance/
END:VEVENT
