DESCRIPTION:Knowing is Doing: Understanding Artist Rights\, is an interactive workshop that equips artists\, students\, and cultural practitioners with the knowledge and tools to navigate the legal\, ethical\, and professional realities of artistic practice. Through collaborative discussions\, speculative role-playing and practical resources\, participants explore authorship\, contracts\, copyright\, labour\, and advocacy\, leaving with greater confidence to protect both their work and themselves. \n\nThis session is conducted as part of our engagements for the MAP Youth Collective. The MAP Youth Collective is a community for young people (18-25 year olds) to engage with the arts and culture sector. The collective is for\, of and by young people — to explore our shared identities and interests through art.
DTEND:20260829T083000Z
LOCATION:HDFC Ltd Learning Centre\, HDFC Ltd Learning Centre\, Lower Ground Floor\, MAP\, Bengaluru\, India
DTSTART:20260829T063000Z
SUMMARY:Knowing is Doing: Understanding Artist Rights
